/**
 * Static, hand-authored, last-resort offline content bank.
 *
 * WHY THIS EXISTS: the original Python system (harvest_question_bank.py)
 * was never uploaded into this Next.js port, so it could not be ported
 * verbatim as the comments in quiz.ts/caseStudies.ts originally noted.
 * Built directly from this project's own synthesized curriculum content
 * in content/books/, not generated by an LLM. It is used ONLY when both
 * Groq and Cerebras are completely unreachable (see the catch paths in
 * quiz.ts and caseStudies.ts), so a missionary always gets *something*
 * useful rather than a bare error message during a provider outage.
 *
 * NOTE: keyed by module NUMBER, not topic — when modules were reordered
 * and renumbered (2026-07-17, adding modules 26-34), this bank's keys
 * were remapped to match. It still only covers the 25 modules that
 * existed when it was authored (now scattered across 1-29 and 34 in the
 * new numbering) — modules 8, 9, 11, 12, 13, and 30-33 have no offline
 * fallback entry yet, and correctly return null (honest error) rather
 * than serving another module's content, which is exactly the bug this
 * remap fixes. Add entries for the missing numbers when convenient.
 *
 * One quiz question + one case study per module. Deliberately compact
 * — this is a last-resort fallback, not a replacement for live
 * generation, which produces richer, more varied content grounded in
 * the full RAG-retrieved context every time it's available.
 */

